## 6. Define Pull Request Standards

Every pull request should explain what changed and why.

A meaningful description allows reviewers to evaluate the impact without reconstructing the entire development process.

Create:

`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`

```markdown
## Summary

Describe the purpose of this change.

## Related Issue

Reference the relevant issue, if applicable.

## Changes

- [ ] Explain the functionality added or changed
- [ ] Update relevant documentation
- [ ] Identify any configuration changes

## Testing

- [ ] Unit tests pass
- [ ] Integration tests pass where applicable
- [ ] Manual testing completed where needed

## Security and Privacy

- [ ] No credentials or sensitive information included
- [ ] Authorization behavior reviewed
- [ ] Health-related data handling reviewed if applicable

## Compatibility

Describe breaking changes, database migrations,
or deployment considerations.
```

Reviewers should prioritize correctness, maintainability, testing, security, and clarity.

A pull request should not be approved solely because its formatting is correct.

